 },
 "kind": "statement",
 "title": "Sections of line bundles of degree at least $2g-1$",
 "statement": "Let $k$ be algebraically closed, $C$ a proper smooth connected curve of\ngenus $g$ ([def-sc-genus]) over $k$, and $\\mathcal L$ a line bundle on\n$C$ of degree $d=\\deg\\mathcal L\\ge2g-1$ ([def-sc-pic0]). Then\n$H^1(C,\\mathcal L)=0$ and\n\n$$\nh^0(\\mathcal L):=\\dim_kH^0(C,\\mathcal L)=d+1-g.\n$$",
 "source": {
  "document": "literature/blueprint/master/blueprint/sec-picard-framework/sk-thm-picard-rr/lem-sc-riemann-roch-large-degree.md",
  "place": "node lem-sc-riemann-roch-large-degree, order 717"
 },
 "stmt_deps": [
  "def-sc-genus",
  "def-sc-pic0",
  "def-sc-curves"
 ],
 "proof": [
  {
   "text": "By Serre duality ([thm-sc-serre-duality-curve]),\n\n$$\nH^1(C,\\mathcal L)^{\\vee}\\cong H^0\\bigl(C,\\Omega^1_{C/k}\\otimes\\mathcal L^{-1}\\bigr).\n$$",
   "uses": [
    "thm-sc-serre-duality-curve"
   ],
   "elementary": false
  },
  {
   "text": "Here $\\Omega^1_{C/k}=\\omega_C=\\mathcal O_C(K_C)$ with\n$\\deg K_C=2g-2$ ([lem-sc-canonical-degree]), so, $\\deg$ being a\nhomomorphism on $\\operatorname{Pic}(C)$ ([def-sc-pic0]),\n\n$$\n\\deg\\bigl(\\Omega^1_{C/k}\\otimes\\mathcal L^{-1}\\bigr)=(2g-2)-d\\le-1<0 .\n$$",
   "uses": [
    "lem-sc-canonical-degree",
    "def-sc-pic0"
   ],
   "elementary": false
  },
  {
   "text": "A line bundle of negative degree has no nonzero global sections\n([lem-sc-negative-degree-no-sections]), so the right-hand side vanishes\nand $H^1(C,\\mathcal L)=0$. Since also $H^q(C,\\mathcal L)=0$ for\n$q\\ge2$, Riemann–Roch ([lem-sc-riemann-roch], part (1)) gives\n\n$$\n\\dim_kH^0(C,\\mathcal L)=\\chi(C,\\mathcal L)=d+1-g.\n$$",
   "uses": [
    "lem-sc-negative-degree-no-sections",
    "lem-sc-riemann-roch"
   ],
   "elementary": false
  }
 ],
 "proof_deps": [
  "thm-sc-serre-duality-curve",
  "lem-sc-canonical-degree",
  "def-sc-pic0",
  "lem-sc-negative-degree-no-sections",
  "lem-sc-riemann-roch"
 ],
